ame": "house", "sentiment": "none"}, {"name": "u.s. postal service", "sentiment": "none"}]}, "highlightText": "", "language": "english", "persons": [], "text": "President Donald Trump would be \"open to\" meeting with Amazon (AMZN) Chief Executive Jeff Bezos, White House press secretary Sarah Sanders said Wednesday, though she said she wasn't aware of anything being scheduled. Sanders was responding to a question about meetings Trump has had with executives, including one Wednesday with Apple (AAPL) CEO Tim Cook. Trump has ripped Amazon's deal with the U.S. Postal Service and also criticized the Washington Post, which is owned by Bezos. Sanders said the meeting with Cook was ongoing and that the discussion would focus on trade.\n-Robert Schroeder; 1500ET\n ", "external_links": ["http://www.addthis.com/bookmark.php?v=250"], "published": "2018-04-25T03:00:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-04-25T22:58:10.008+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}